They met in Galilee. Then Jesus said to them, "The Son of Man will be delivered over to the men."
They will kill him. On the third day, he will rise from the dead." The disciples felt great sadness. Jesus pays the temple tax.
Jesus and his disciples arrived in Capernaum. There, a tax collector came to Peter. And they asked him, "Does not your teacher pay the temple tax?"
"Yes, he does," he answered. When Peter went into the house, Jesus spoke first. "What do you think, Simon?" he asked. "On whom do the kings of the earth collect taxes and fees? Do they collect it from their sons or from others?"
"From others," Peter answered. "For children are not to pay," Jesus told him.
But we do not want to anger them. So go to the lake and cast your fishing line. Take the first fish you catch. Open its mouth. There you will find the exact coin you need. Take it and give it to them for each of our taxes.
